{
 "**A subscription.** Nothing renews by itself.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Accessibility.** Every accessibility setting is free, and so are the Wardrobe pieces that help, such as the calm celebration and the contrast plates.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Adverts:** the only third party in the game is Google’s advertising service, and it runs only when a player chooses to watch a video. Video adverts are limited to Google’s general-audience content rating. If iOS asks whether OutBrick may track, **Ask App Not to Track** leaves the game unchanged. In the EU, the UK and Switzerland, a consent form appears before the first video, and **Settings › Game › Advertising choices** reopens it.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Ask before buying.** If a button shows a price in pounds, dollars, euros or any other money, it costs real money. Ask a grown-up first.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Between boards is the perfect place to stop.** On Home or the map, nothing is in progress.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Chance.** There are no loot boxes and no mystery packs. Every paid item says exactly what it contains, and the Brick Wheel never takes money.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Choose a stopping point before you start**, such as the end of a village, and let the village celebration be your cue.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Delete My Data** cannot be undone. After using it, another device signed in to the same iCloud may sync an older save back, so use it on every device if you mean to start over. See [Progress, iCloud and privacy](help:progress-privacy-and-account#delete).": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "**Delete My Data**, at the foot of **Settings › Game**, resets the device’s progress and asks iCloud to delete the save. See [Progress, iCloud and privacy](help:progress-privacy-and-account#delete).": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Game Center** is Apple’s service. It keeps your 65 achievements and the leaderboards for highest level, total clears, today and this week.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "**Game Center** is optional and run by Apple, under your Game Center settings.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Give up** ends the attempt and uses a life.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Haptics** are the small taps you feel as pieces move and land. The switch only appears on devices that can vibrate.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**If a board frustrates you, leave it for today.** Lives refill, the helping hand arrives, and boards often look different after a rest.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**In the middle of a board**, tap **Pause**. **Resume** brings you straight back.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Keep your name secret.** Pick a made-up player name, not your real one.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Leaving before your first move is always free.** After a move, the **Leave?** card tells you a life will be used before you choose.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Lives are used by losing, not by playing.** Opening a board needs a life but does not use one. A life is used when an attempt is lost: giving up when the moves run out, or restarting or leaving after making a move, and the game says so before it happens. Winning never costs a life, and lives come back on their own, one every 30 minutes.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Lives refill on their own**, one every 30 minutes, even while the game is closed. Tap the heart on the Journey to see when the next one comes.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Look before you move.** Find the gates and the goals first. The order panel at the top tells you what the board wants.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Losing costs a life; playing and winning do not.** Lives come back on their own, one every 30 minutes.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Losing is all right.** If you run out of moves, you can try again. A heart goes when you lose, and hearts come back by themselves.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Missions.** They pay coins, boosters and tokens, and never sell anything.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**No account to create.** Progress is saved on the device and in your family’s own iCloud. OutBrick has no analytics, and the developer does not receive gameplay data.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**No accounts and no analytics.** The developer does not receive gameplay data.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**No adverts unless your child taps to watch one.** There are no banners and no adverts between boards. A video only plays when a player presses a button to watch one for a reward, each kind is capped every day (39 in total), and a video can always be declined at no cost.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**No chat, no strangers.** There is no chat, no messaging between players and nothing written by other players inside the game. Other players can only ever see a player name and level (more on that [below](#other-players)).": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Nothing is a subscription, and nothing paid appears on a board before level 6.**": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Nothing is a subscription.** Every purchase is a one-time purchase through Apple, nothing renews by itself, and nothing paid is offered on a board before level 6.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Paying removes videos, never rewards.** Remove Ads and the Brick Pass pay the same rewards without the video.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Pressure on new players.** Nothing paid is offered on a board before level 6.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Progress** is stored on the device and synced through your own iCloud, which the developer cannot read.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Purchases** are processed by Apple. OutBrick never sees or stores card details.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Remove Ads**, or holding the current season’s Brick Pass, stops the game asking for adverts at all, and the rewards still pay.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Replay a cleared board** from the map when you want something familiar. Replaying never moves your place on the Journey.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Reviews.** There is no reward for rating the game.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Running out of moves is not the end.** You can play on with coins, with a video, or simply try again.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Settings › Game › Game features** switches off **Friend Rescue**, **Village Race**, **Brick Royale**, **Crew Race** and **Offers on the map**. Nothing you have earned is lost.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Settings › Screen Time › App Limits › Add Limit.** Choose the **Games** category, or OutBrick on its own, and a daily amount. When the time is up, iOS covers the game.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Settings › Screen Time › Downtime.** A scheduled quiet time, such as bedtime, when only the apps you allow can open.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Something feels wrong?** Stop and tell a grown-up.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Sounds**, **Music** and **Haptics** each have their own switch in **Settings › Game**, and the same three are in the **Pause** menu, so you can change them in the middle of a board.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Take breaks.** The game waits for you. The friends will still be there when you come back.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Take your time.** There is no clock. Think as long as you like before every move.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**There is no clock anywhere.** No board, menu or event is timed. The number of moves is the only limit, so nobody is ever hurried.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Time.** There is no clock to buy your way past.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Undo freely, once.** The first undo on every board is free.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Use the free Hint.** It is there on every attempt and cannot be saved, so using it costs nothing.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Videos are always your choice.** There are eight kinds, each with a daily limit, 39 in all. Nothing plays by itself.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Videos are your choice.** A video only plays if you tap a button to watch one. You can always say no.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Village Race** and **Brick Royale** share the player name with the other players in that race, and only when your child joins one. Each can be switched off in **Settings › Game › Game features**, along with Friend Rescue, Crew Race and offers on the map.": "help:parents-guide",
 "**Your data.** We do not sell or share personal information for money.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "**Your day streak can wait.** A streak of three days or more can be restored within a week of a missed day, free with a streak saver or for 250 coins.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "**Your progress is safe.** It is saved as you go, on the device and in iCloud.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "A **Focus filter** can turn off the music, pause reminders and hide the badge while a Focus such as Sleep is on. See [Playing calmly](help:playing-calmly#reminders).": "help:parents-guide",
 "A **community account** keeps a public display name and a private email address, which is never shown to anyone.": "help:parents-guide",
 "A Focus filter for OutBrick": "help:playing-calmly",
 "A Focus filter never changes your own settings. While one is at work, a line under **Music** in Settings says so.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "A blue brick with a wristwatch on a lanyard. Bloo checks the time between boards and spins when you clear one: first to wave, first to try the bold move, and quite sure he meant to do that.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A checklist to work through": "help:parents-guide",
 "A dark green brick with a tool belt and muddy work boots, and a farm saying for every weather. Moss saves one slow clap for when you have earned it, so it counts.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A friend celebrates on the win card, and a friend commiserates on **Level failed** when a board gets away from you.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A gentler screen": "help:playing-calmly",
 "A guide for parents and carers": "help:parents-guide",
 "A member’s email address is never shown to anyone. Every post is public and moderated, and anything that breaks the [guidelines](/community/guidelines) can be reported.": "help:parents-guide",
 "A pale blue brick in a striped bobble hat and scarf, fond of tea and a gentle wave. Flurry is never in a hurry, which suits a game with no clock. Watch the scarf: its tail always swings a beat late.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A peach-coloured brick with a little peach on top. Peach counts the moves twice, keeps a backup plan and frets the whole way through, then cheers when the pile finally opens.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A pink brick with a star-tipped wand. To Poppy, every board is the middle of a fairy tale, and the ending is when the wand bursts into stars.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A purple brick in headphones who hears a rhythm in a good run of moves. Vio rates your moves like tracks, grooves along at 112 beats a minute, and treats a tidy clear as a five-star track.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A quieter game": "help:playing-calmly",
 "A red brick in big red boots who treats every board like a set at the gym. Bricko counts his reps, and a clear gets a thumbs-up and a flex, in that order.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A saved **+5 moves** can be used here too. Brick Pass owners get **three free moves** here as well.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "A small green brick with a seedling on top. Sprout notices the gap everyone else walked past and asks the question nobody else did. When it works, two hops and a spin.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "A yellow brick with a ready wink. Zippy starts a thought, loses the thread halfway, and comes back for the win. A poke gets a spin; a win gets a triple hop.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Add your device, iOS version and OutBrick version. The game’s version is at the foot of your **Profile** (tap your avatar).": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "After that, undos come from a tank of up to **5**, which refills by **one every 25 minutes**.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Also under **Motion**. Full-screen flashes from big combos drop to a third of their strength and never come closer together than about a third of a second.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "An unexpected or duplicate charge goes the same way: check **Purchase History** first, then Report a Problem. More on our [refunds page](/refunds).": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "App Limits": "help:parents-guide",
 "Apple occasionally renames rows between iOS versions. If a name on your device differs slightly from the one here, look for the closest match under **Content & Privacy Restrictions**.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Apple takes every payment for OutBrick, so Apple alone decides refunds. We cannot see your payment details or refund an App Store purchase.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Apple takes every payment, so only Apple can refund one. Go to [reportaproblem.apple.com](https://reportaproblem.apple.com), sign in with the Apple Account used for the purchase, choose **Request a refund**, and pick the OutBrick item. Apple decides, under its rules and your local consumer law. We cannot see your payment details or issue an App Store refund ourselves. More on our [refunds page](/refunds) and in [Lost progress or a missing purchase](help:lost-progress-and-purchases#refunds).": "help:parents-guide",
 "Apple, at [reportaproblem.apple.com](https://reportaproblem.apple.com). We cannot see payments or refund them. If something bought did not arrive, try **Restore Purchase** at the foot of the Shop first, then [write to us](/contact?topic=purchases).": "help:parents-guide",
 "Apple’s service for achievements, leaderboards and friends. Its friend and multiplayer settings sit in **Screen Time › Content & Privacy Restrictions**, in the Game Center section.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Ask to Buy (Family Sharing)": "help:parents-guide",
 "Because no board is timed, OutBrick is easy to put down: nothing is lost by stopping between boards, and lives keep refilling while the game is closed. If you would like a firmer edge to play time, Apple’s Screen Time does it well.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Before you switch, open OutBrick once on the **old** device while signed in to iCloud.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Beyond the game": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Bloo, Peach and Sprout": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Bloo, Peach, Sprout, Bricko, Zippy, Vio, Moss, Flurry and Poppy: who each friend is, how they show it, and everywhere you meet them in OutBrick.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Bloo, the one with the watch": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Both take the videos away **without taking the rewards**: every button that said Watch says **Claim reward** instead, and pays at once, within the same daily limits. Paying never costs you a reward.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Bricko, Zippy and Vio": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Bricko, the one doing reps": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Bring back a purchase": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Bring back a purchase with Restore Purchase, what to send us if it is still missing, how Apple handles refunds, and how to recover progress through iCloud, on a new iPhone or iPad, and with Game Center.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "By the third play-on, refilling a whole tank of lives (600 coins) and starting fresh costs less than another 900 coins of moves. The game would rather you started again calmly than kept paying to stand still.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
