 "I bought Remove Ads. Do I lose the free lives and moves the videos gave?": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "I reinstalled OutBrick and I am back at level 1.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "If a device was never signed in to iCloud, its progress exists only on that device. Sign in to iCloud there and open OutBrick once, then check the other device again.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "If another device has the progress you expect, open OutBrick there too, online, so it can share its save.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "If no move is possible, the board reshuffles for free. You can never be truly stuck.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "If something was bought by mistake": "help:parents-guide",
 "If you think a child has made an account, tell us through the [contact form](/contact) and we will delete it.": "help:parents-guide",
 "If your child has their own Apple Account in your Family Sharing group, Ask to Buy sends every purchase request, including purchases inside games, to you to approve or decline.": "help:parents-guide",
 "In OutBrick **Settings › Accessibility**: 50%, 75%, 100%, 150% or 200%. At 75% or 50%, swaps, falls and clears play more slowly and are easier to follow.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "In the game, **Settings › Game › Notifications** turns them all off. On the iPhone, **Settings › Notifications › OutBrick** controls them and the icon badge.": "help:parents-guide",
 "In the iPhone **Settings › Accessibility › Motion**. Idle movement on the board stops, glows hold still, hints shimmer in place, screens cross-fade instead of sliding, and every win celebration turns to a soft glow.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "In the iPhone **Settings › Focus**, choose a Focus, such as Sleep or Personal.": "help:playing-calmly",
