 "Opening a board needs a life, but **does not use one**.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Or watch an **optional video**: **+2 moves**, then **+1 move**, then a **free UFO**. A video never pushes the coin price up.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Other players and the community": "help:parents-guide",
 "Out of lives? Once a day you may get a **free try** at a board. Otherwise you can wait, refill the whole tank for **600 coins**, watch a video for **1 life**, or buy unlimited lives: **1 hour for 900 coins**, **3 hours for 2,000** or **24 hours for 6,000**, or with real money in the Shop.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "OutBrick has **nine brick friends**, each a toy brick with a colour, a look and a way of celebrating all of their own. They keep you company on Home and on every board, and they show how they feel through how they move and what appears in their text bubbles.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "OutBrick has **no forced adverts**: no banners, no adverts between boards, nothing that plays by itself. A video only starts when you tap a button to watch one, and only a video watched to the end pays. Each kind has its own daily limit, and the limits reset at midnight.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "OutBrick has a Messages app for sending a level challenge or a sticker to someone your child already messages. Screen Time’s **Communication Limits** apply to it as to any conversation.": "help:parents-guide",
 "OutBrick is a calm slide-and-match puzzle, rated **4+** on the App Store. Players move toy bricks into gates of their own colour, or swap neighbours to make lines, and each board gives a number of moves to do it in. Before you reach for any setting, here is what the game does and does not do.": "help:parents-guide",
 "OutBrick never asks for notification permission when it first opens. After the third clear it asks whether Bloo may keep your place, and **Not now** waits a week.": "help:parents-guide",
 "OutBrick reminders": "help:parents-guide",
 "OutBrick sends **at most one notification every 20 hours**, and **never between 22:00 and 09:00**. Each offers **Play**, **Later** (three hours) or **Tomorrow**.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Outfits for the friends, such as King Bricko’s gold crown and red ruff. Wardrobe pieces change how the game looks, never how it plays.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Peach, the careful planner": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Player name": "help:parents-guide",
 "Playing calmly": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Playing on with coins, within one attempt": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Please do not. Never post a receipt in the community. Use the private [contact form](/contact?topic=purchases), and leave out card numbers, passwords and security codes.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Please leave your child’s personal details out of support messages. A level number and the device are all we need.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Poppy, the storyteller": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Prices are shown in your own currency in the Shop. Neither one renews by itself. See [The Shop, purchases and restoring](help:shop-and-purchases#remove-ads) and [the Brick Pass](help:rewards-and-events#pass).": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Progress is missing": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Purchases: Ask to Buy, restrictions and refunds": "help:parents-guide",
 "Questions parents ask": "help:parents-guide",
 "Races": "help:parents-guide",
 "Reading the website needs no account. Visits are measured with Google Analytics **only if you accept it** in the cookie banner; until then nothing loads from Google.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Real-money items appear in the **Shop** and on a few cards in the game, always with a price in your own currency, and always through Apple’s own purchase sheet. Two Apple controls decide whether that sheet can complete.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Refunds are Apple’s": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Running out of moves": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Say **what you bought** and **when**, roughly is fine.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Say “Meet Bloo in OutBrick” to Siri (or any friend’s name), find a friend in Spotlight, add the **Mascot of the Day** or **Mascot Mood** widget, or send a friend’s sticker in Messages.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Saying no to a video costs nothing.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Send it. A person reads every message, and you get an email with a reference and a private link.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Set **Animation speed** to 75% or 50% in **Settings › Accessibility**. For less movement everywhere, turn on **Reduce Motion** in the iPhone Settings.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Set **In-app Purchases** to **Don’t Allow**. While you are there, set **Require Password** to **Always Require**.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Set a **Screen Time passcode** that your child does not know, so these choices stay as you left them.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Set in the Profile (tap the avatar). A made-up name is a good idea.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Setting up OutBrick for a child": "help:parents-guide",
 "Settings on the Game tab: On switches for Notifications, Sounds, Music, Quick play and Mascot AI chatter, each with a line explaining it, then buttons for Game features, Rate OutBrick, Contact us, Community, Report a bug and Support.": "help:playing-calmly · help:settings",
 "Settings › Accessibility. Animation speed is at the top.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Settings › Game.": "help:playing-calmly · help:settings",
 "Should I post my receipt so you can check it?": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Show me on the standings board": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Sign in to Game Center in the iPhone Settings with the same Apple Account to see your achievements again.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Sign in with the Apple Account used for the purchase.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Someone asked for my Apple Account password to fix my purchase.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Sound, music and haptics": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Sound, music, haptics, notifications and most board accessibility settings stay on each device, so set them again on the new one. Your colour-blind choice travels with your progress.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Sprout, the one with questions": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "Start here": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Stay online for a minute with iCloud on and the same Apple Account. If nothing changes, the earlier progress may have been on a device that was not signed in to iCloud: see [Progress is missing](#progress).": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Stepping away without losing anything": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Still missing: write to us": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Struggling with one board? From your sixth attempt at it, the game gives you **3 extra moves** before you start, once a day per board. Sometimes the calmest move is to come back tomorrow.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Stuck?": "help:parents-guide",
 "Submit it, and check its status with Apple. Approval and timing are set by Apple and your local consumer law.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Tank empty? Buy **5 for 250 coins**, watch a video for **2**, or wait.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Tap **Add Filter**, then **OutBrick**.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "Tap **Ask to Buy** and turn it on.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Tap **Content & Privacy Restrictions** and turn it on.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Tap **iTunes & App Store Purchases**.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Tap the **Hint** in the tray at the bottom. You get one free on every try.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Tap your child’s name.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Ten minutes with your child’s device and your own covers everything. Print this page, or tick the boxes in your head.": "help:parents-guide",
 "Text bubbles and Mascot AI chatter": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "That was not us. We never ask for your Apple Account password or card details. Do not share them, and tell us through the [contact form](/contact).": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "The **Leaders** tab in the game is a separate, all-time board. You appear on it while **Settings › Game › Show me on the standings board** is on.": "help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "The **contact form** keeps what you send so we can answer it. A support case is kept for 24 months after it is closed, then deleted.": "help:parents-guide",
 "The **first undo on every board is free**, and never runs out.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "The **icon badge** counts rewards waiting for you, up to nine. Opening the game clears it without claiming anything. To hide it for good, turn off **Badges** in **Settings › Notifications › OutBrick**.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "The **icon badge** counts rewards waiting to be collected, up to nine. It is only shown if notifications are allowed, and opening the game clears it.": "help:parents-guide",
 "The Accessibility tab: Animation speed from 50% to 200%, Announcement detail Brief, Standard or Full, and switches for Colour-blind, High-contrast board, Left-handed tray, Hold to confirm swaps and Row sound.": "help:playing-calmly · help:settings",
 "The Ring/Silent switch and the volume buttons work as usual.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "The Seasonal Cards, nine to a season, show the friends.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "The Shop. Every real-money item goes through Apple’s purchase sheet.": "help:parents-guide",
 "The Undo button counts both, so a fresh board shows **6** when your tank is full.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "The community is a forum on this website, **separate from the game**. Anyone can read it; posting needs an account, and accounts are for people **aged 16 and over**.": "help:parents-guide",
 "The eight optional videos": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "The friends cheer you on in text bubbles. On devices with Apple’s on-device language model, they can also make up their own lines: **Settings › Game › Mascot AI chatter**, shown only where the model is available in your language. It runs entirely on your device, and turning it off brings back their usual lines.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "The friends never speak aloud. Everything they have to say appears in a text bubble, so nothing about them depends on hearing.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "The friends talk in **text bubbles**, never aloud, and nothing in the game depends on hearing. Playing in silence loses nothing.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "The kindest stopping point is between boards, on Home or the map. Leaving a board before the first move is always free; after a move, the **Leave?** card says a life will be used before anything happens.": "help:parents-guide",
 "The price goes back to 300 coins with every new attempt, when you leave the board, or when you clear it. It never climbs past 900.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "The settings that make OutBrick quieter and gentler, why there is never a clock, how to step away without losing anything, and a few habits for unhurried play.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "The two refills, lives and undos, are flat prices. They never go up however often you need them.": "help:rewards-and-ads",
 "The village’s host friend sits in the round frame in the header, dressed for that village. Tap them for a giggle, a wave or a high-five.": "help:meet-the-friends",
 "There is never a clock": "help:playing-calmly",
 "There is nothing to switch off: no board in OutBrick has a timer. Moves are the only limit.": "help:playing-calmly",
 "They speak in text bubbles only, so everything they say can be read, and nothing depends on hearing.": "help:meet-the-friends",
